import CFSGOutside.Corpus.Defs.OpenVocabulary

/-!
# Corpus input: MacWilliams's four-generator theorem

Statement of `CFSG.Milestones.cls_connectivity_macwilliams_four_generator`
(`CFSG/Milestones/CLS_connectivity_MacWilliams_four_generator.lean`, line 11, at AxiomMath/CFSG commit
69cb972f587a3ecc035e092253167ff2e303c962), copied verbatim. The theorem is stated inside `namespace CFSG.Open`,
so its `IsElemAbelian` is `CFSG.Open.IsElemAbelian`, copied as `CFSGOutside.Corpus.Open.IsElemAbelian`. Its proof
is `CFSG.LargeEvenClassification.Helpers.macwilliams_four_generators`
(`CFSG/LocalAnalysis/LargeEvenClassification/MacWilliamsFull.lean`).

A finite 2-group with no normal elementary abelian subgroup of order 8 has every subgroup generated by at most
four elements (MacWilliams 1970: such a group has sectional 2-rank at most 4). The clean build provides the
instance in `clean/CFSGOutsideClean/Corpus/MacWilliamsFourGenerator.lean`.
-/

namespace CFSGOutside.Corpus

/-- MacWilliams's four-generator theorem, as `cls_connectivity_macwilliams_four_generator` states it. -/
class MacWilliamsFourGenerator : Prop where
  cls_connectivity_macwilliams_four_generator :
    ∀ (S : Type) [Group S] [Finite S] (_hS : IsPGroup 2 S)
      (_hE : ∀ E : Subgroup S, E.Normal → Open.IsElemAbelian 2 E → Nat.card E ≠ 8),
      ∀ U : Subgroup S, ∃ X : Finset S, X.card ≤ 4 ∧ Subgroup.closure (X : Set S) = U

end CFSGOutside.Corpus
